From 4826ca5a9225ec826182625be02cb6c31b4d25d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:19:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 112/165] net: qrtr: Send HELLO early when a packet waits for
 it

qrtr_node_enqueue() drops every non-HELLO packet to a node until our
HELLO to it has gone out, and that HELLO is sent from a work item that
backs off for 100 ms whenever sending it fails.

If the remote's HELLO arrives in that window, the name server's
announcements of the local services are dropped and announce_servers()
gives up, so the remote never learns about them. On Kaanapali the modem
then can't find its remote file system and its watchdog fires.

When a packet hits the gate, run the pending HELLO work right away and
check again.

Fixes: 544d85de4dc2 ("net: qrtr: Send HELLO message on endpoint register")

[ from infiniti-mainline/linux master, commit 839c154d7e75 ]
[ upstream author: Victor Fuentes <victor@vlinkz.dev>; picked for the iceland kernel q89 ]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c b/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c
index e7b3647424b8..d79bc99ded17 100644
--- a/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c
+++ b/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c
@@ -352,8 +352,19 @@ static int qrtr_node_enqueue(struct qrtr_node *node, struct sk_buff *skb,
 	mutex_lock(&node->ep_lock);
 	if (!node->hello_sent && type != QRTR_TYPE_HELLO) {
 		mutex_unlock(&node->ep_lock);
-		kfree_skb(skb);
-		return -EAGAIN;
+
+		/* Our HELLO may still be backing off while the remote
+		 * already talks to us: send it now.
+		 */
+		mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &node->say_hello, 0);
+		flush_delayed_work(&node->say_hello);
+
+		mutex_lock(&node->ep_lock);
+		if (!node->hello_sent) {
+			mutex_unlock(&node->ep_lock);
+			kfree_skb(skb);
+			return -EAGAIN;
+		}
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&node->ep_lock);
 
-- 
